# EchoCast Receiver package output.
#
# A built package is ~250 MB, most of it a GPL FFmpeg binary, and it is
# reproducible from the spec plus a named FFmpeg source. Committing it would
# put a third-party binary into this repository's history permanently, where
# removing it later means rewriting history.
artifacts/
build/pyi-dist/
build/pyi-work/
*.exe
!scripts/*.exe
build/pyi-dist-*/
build/pyi-work-*/

# ==================================================
# Repo-native HQ runtime (tools/echocast_server.py)
# ==================================================
# The repository IS the installation, so HQ's live data sits in <repo>/data
# for operator simplicity - one folder to back up. None of it may ever be
# committed: it is the database, the signing secret, the Receiver key
# container, the logs and the PID/runtime state of a real installation.
# The CONTENTS are ignored rather than the directory itself: git does not
# descend into an ignored directory, so `/data/` followed by `!data/.gitkeep`
# silently keeps the placeholder out too, and a fresh clone then has no data
# folder at all.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep

# Broadcast recordings. Already covered by /data/* above; named explicitly
# because these are recordings of real announcements in real shops, and
# "it happens to be under an ignored directory" is a weaker guarantee than
# saying so. Never commit one.
/data/recordings/
**/recordings/*.webm
**/recordings/*.webm.part

# Test audio fixtures are GENERATED, never committed. The repository refuses
# to track audio at all (test_repository_contains_no_committed_audio_artifact),
# and a synthetic tone is no exception - it is built by FFmpeg on demand.
/frontend/e2e/fixtures/

# Belt and braces for the individual kinds, in case a data directory is
# relocated with ECHOCAST_DATA_DIR and ends up somewhere else in the tree.
**/echocast.db
**/echocast.db-wal
**/echocast.db-shm
**/receiver-hmac-keys.bin
**/jwt-secret.txt
**/settings-password.json
**/hq.pid
**/hq-state.json
**/requirements.stamp

# The one tracked thing under data/, so the folder exists in a fresh clone.

# Generated MediaRecorder captures for the WebM framer tests. The repository
# tracks no audio artifacts; these are produced on demand by
# "ECHOCAST_CAPTURE_WEBM=1 npx playwright test e2e/capture-fixture.spec.js".
/backend/tests/fixtures/mediarecorder-live.webm
/backend/tests/fixtures/mediarecorder-live.chunks.json
/frontend/build-e2e/

# Isolated verification builds. Never the live HQ frontend.
frontend/build-dev/
